    "result_text": "Those are just the new `luhnCheckDigit` helper \u2014 no stale references remain. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single **`memberId`** formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. All 68 tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single `memberId` property, and removed the `checkDigit` property. The generated `OwnerDto` picks these up at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 Removed the `customer_code` and `membership_number` fields and their accessors; added a `member_id` field with `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Replaced `generateCustomerCode`/`generateMembershipNumber`/`deduplicateCustomerCode` with `generateMemberId`/`deduplicateMemberId` plus a `luhnCheckDigit` helper. The id is built as `region + FY2 + HASH8 + CHK`, where `HASH8` is the same SHA-256-over-`(telephone+lastName)` first-8-hex used by the region-and-hash identity, `FY2` is the 2-digit fiscal year, and `CHK` is a Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Collision handling now de-duplicates the `memberId`.\n   - Updated both audit outputs (human line and structured `OWNER_CREATED` event) to reference `memberId` instead of the removed fields.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Removed the `checkDigit` mapping and the now-unused `luhnCheckDigit`; updated `deriveLocality` (which feeds `ownerSegment`'s AREA and `timezone`) to read the region prefix from `memberId` instead of the old customer code. `memberId` maps automatically by name.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Replaced the `customer_code` and `membership_number` columns with a single `member_id` column.\n\nThe `fiscalYear` field remains an `FY<YY>` value; its 2-digit year is now also embedded inside `memberId`, matching the spec.",
